thread:
anya: Heads-up — we need a contract for the rollout metrics that runtime and infra will emit so Analytics/Console can render the 1k-token cost + breakdowns. Anyone owning the schema?
kevin: I can drive schema but need clear runtime fields: tokens_in, tokens_out, model_variant, kv_cache_hits, batch_count, batch_size, gpu_ms, fallback_model, region.
eva: analytics: Need per-route tags + rate-limits + pricing_tier to compute cost per 1k and attribution.
josh: runtime: We can emit token events and aggregated counters. Concern: extra telemetry volume. Propose minimal per-request payload + 1m rollups.
anya: Prefer both: per-request minimal fields for debugging + 1min rollup sums for dashboards.
maria: console: Also need rollout metadata: canary_id, rollout_percent, policy (latency/cost) so UI shows which cohort.
sam: eng-infra: How do we correlate across layers? Add `request_id`, `deployment_id`, `region`, `model_version`.
kevin: Agreed. Quick proto sketch below — minimal and rollup-friendly: 
```
message InferenceTelemetry {
  string request_id = 1;
  string deployment_id = 2;
  string model = 3;
  string model_variant = 4;
  int32 tokens_in = 5;
  int32 tokens_out = 6;
  int32 batch_size = 7;
  int32 kv_cache_hits = 8;
  double gpu_ms = 9;
  string route = 10;
  string pricing_tier = 11;
  string canary_id = 12;
  int32 rollout_pct = 13;
}
```
eva: For dashboards we'll compute: 
- `cost_per_1k` = (sum(gpu_ms * gpu_cost_per_ms) + infra_share) / sum(tokens_out) * 1000
- `cache_savings_pct` = 1 - (tokens_out_with_cache / tokens_out_no_cache)
We also need `avg_batch_tokens`, `p95_latency_per_batch`.
kevin: Also add a `BatchBreakdown` event with `batch_latency_ms` and `items` to help attribute savings to batching.
josh: Implementation note: KV cache hit will be a count at request level (kv_cache_hits) not per-token. That should be fine for rollups.
anya: Timeline? Need UI prototype by next Wed for PM review.
maria: Can we include sample rollup payloads? For UI we need per-route and per-model time series + canary cohorts.
sam: We'll ensure ingestion supports 1m rollups and backfills. We may need sampling for high-traffic routes to control carding costs.
kevin: I'll open a PR with the proto + ingest contract by EOD tomorrow and add example query templates.
deploy-bot: deploy-bot: New PR opened by kevin: https://git.internal/r/1234 
eva: I'll start mock queries against the example data once PR lands. Will add expected chart specs.
anya: Thanks team — please ping here with blockers. :thumbsup:
